Implement the libssh2 CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6 in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift), backed by libssh2. Package libssh2 (pinned per TASK-260715-28ok1k: commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend, Apache-2.0) as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt native seam + rebuild hook (checksum-verify pinned source; ADR-019). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary as a NAMED adapter module (libssh2/OpenSSL imported ONLY here; NOT in ReluxTunnelCore proper — make validate-core enforces). KEY FIT (why libssh2 suits the neutral seam where NIOSSH did not): drive libssh2 over the injected neutral SSHTCPConnection (readySome/readSome/writeSome/close) using libssh2 CUSTOM TRANSPORT send/recv callbacks (libssh2_session_callback_set) in NONBLOCKING mode (EAGAIN) — no socket/descriptor ownership needed, so the injected/fakeable connector (E-INJECTION) works. IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (libssh2 hostkey + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy before credential lookup; changed-key stop); public-key auth via an EXTERNAL SIGNER (libssh2_userauth_publickey sign-callback — private key NEVER exported, stays with the caller); openDirectTCPIP (libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex); openExecChannel (exec); upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); PER-CHANNEL window via libssh2_channel_open_ex(window_size)+window_read_ex+receive_window_adjust2 with CONSUMER-DRIVEN credit (return credit only after the API read consumes bytes — libssh2 lets the adapter own credit return, satisfying contract section 9 backpressure and maximumBufferedReadBytes); client REKEY by byte/time threshold scheduled by the adapter (libssh2 has no auto-rekey threshold — see audit); keepalive (libssh2_keepalive) with RTT; bounded IO/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics; report exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC. UNIT-TEST driven over an in-memory/loopback byte seam (no live SSH fixtures — those are 39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/scale is 1u2vpc, P0-gated). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer). Build+test via swift build/test on macOS. If a contract clause genuinely cannot be satisfied by libssh2 public API, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (that would signal a contract revision, a bigger decision) — do not force-fit.--- task projection ---
id:TASK-260715-1ozsb6
name:integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter
status:development
description:Implement the libssh2 candidate adapter behind the revised M0-viability SSH transport contract, including nonblocking socket integration and bounded async adaptation, and build it in the macOS harness and the macOS provider configuration. libssh2 is the human-approved primary candidate (2026-07-28). The four semantics deferred to M3 are surfaced as explicit not-reported or unsupported states, never fabricated values, and never silent fallbacks.
scope:In scope: pinned libssh2 and crypto backend; extension-safe static or source build; session handshake; raw host-key access before authentication; approved public-key auth; direct-tcpip; bidirectional exec and exec/stdin upload; client-initiated rekey trigger; nonblocking EAGAIN integration; bounded buffers; deterministic cancellation and timeouts; keepalive; cheaply-available metrics; privacy-safe error mapping; allocator hooks where supported; macOS harness registration; macOS provider configuration build. Out of scope: iOS simulator and iPhone provider configurations (iOS deferred); consumer-driven receive-window credit semantics, RFC channel-open reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit metadata, and deep rekey/keepalive observability (all owned by the M3 task); NIOSSH fork work; masking an unsupported viability gate without a recorded decision; blocking calls on provider executors; SFTP; password prompts; ProxyJump; agent forwarding; production lane scheduling; candidate types outside the adapter.
ac:1. The M0-viability tier adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for the macOS harness and macOS provider configuration and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence before authentication, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, exec/stdin upload, client rekey, server-rekey handling, bounded buffers, keepalive, available metrics, Keychain-only secret references, and privacy-safe errors satisfy every M0-viability-mandatory row or remain red with reproducible evidence. 4. The four M3-deferred semantics are emitted as explicit not-reported or unsupported states and are traceable to TASK-260728-3cveay; no deferred value is fabricated. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.
